  "security_implications": "out_q resets to 1, which may enable key manager configuration before software explicitly sets vld_set and without a vld_dis assertion. This could allow early, unauthorized access to key slots or key generation if the keymgr is operational after reset. The highest-priority disable input (vld_dis) can mitigate this if asserted externally, but its default absence leaves a window of potential exposure. A security review should confirm whether the default-enabled state is acceptable or if the reset value should be 0 to require an explicit enable.",
